However:

> They've made
> up their mind and don't care about any opinion but their own, while
> walking around with an air of "Oh, look, we talk to the players."

is nonsense. I will mention three things we have adopted from player
input, without much changing:

* introducing Trog's highest power Brothers in Arms (cyrus)
* change the praying model completely (Iainuki)
* make races easier according to player wishes (Demigod, Kenku etc.)

And you can follow Crawl development on the Sourceforge page: we take
our players seriously, but of course we have to rule. Having each and
every one have their say would lead to a halt. By the way, I do not
see what's wrong with players being testers.

A much more valid point would be: "They are abusing the players as
idea-cows, without having them participate in the decision process."
While I would not phrase it like that, this is much closer to the
truth: we (the team) look at the proposals with voracious interest. We
discuss, adapt and take the ideas we like; and we comment on and skip
others (even if they are good, there may be several reasons not to
implement some). And of course, there is no committee. Design is not
decided in a democratic process.

